WEBVTT

1
00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:47.375
<b>In the previous two verses,</b>

2
00:00:47.375 --> 00:00:55.208
<b>Lord Krishna describedthe characteristics and </b>
<b>qualities of a spiritually advanced Karma Yogi.</b>

3
00:00:55.208 --> 00:00:58.958
<b>From here, Lord Krishna will introduce</b>
<b>the concept of sacrifice,</b>

4
00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.791
<b>the ultimate result of which is to attain knowledge,</b>

5
00:01:01.791 --> 00:01:05.750
<b>and this concept will continue for </b>
<b>the next several verses.</b>

6
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.833
<b>In these twenty-third and twenty-fourth verses</b>
<b>of the fourth chapter, Krishna explains</b>

7
00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:13.291
<b>that for the person who has</b>
<b>attained divine knowledge,</b>

8
00:01:13.291 --> 00:01:18.750
<b>the material results of their actions give </b>
<b>birth to neither sin nor virtue,</b>

9
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.166
<b>but their actions themselves become </b>
<b>a means of their purification.</b>

10
00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:28.125
<b>And how this happens is described </b>
<b>in these two verses.</b>

11
00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.041
<b>In the twenty-third verse, Lord Krishna says</b>

12
00:01:35.041 --> 00:01:37.458
<b>that the person who is free from attachments,</b>

13
00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:39.958
<b>whose mind is established in divine knowledge,</b>

14
00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:45.208
<b>performs all his duties with a sense </b>
<b>of renunciation and dedication,</b>

15
00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:50.375
<b>and by doing so, he becomes free from </b>
<b>all the fruits of that action.</b>

16
00:01:50.375 --> 00:01:57.041
<b>The actions of such a person begin in </b>
<b>the spiritual and dissolve in the spiritual itself.</b>

17
00:01:57.041 --> 00:02:02.250
<b>This is explained through these </b>
<b>three words in this verse:</b>

18
00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.166
<b>First -</b>

19
00:02:03.166 --> 00:02:05.500
<b>gatasaṅgasya muktasya –</b>

20
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.291
<b>meaning separate from the material world – </b>

21
00:02:09.291 --> 00:02:13.208
<b>such a person has no attachment </b>
<b>to the material world,</b>

22
00:02:13.208 --> 00:02:17.666
<b>he is not influenced by any of the </b>
<b>three modes of nature.</b>

23
00:02:17.666 --> 00:02:22.041
<b>He is neither influenced by tamas, </b>
<b>i.e., laziness and ignorance,</b>

24
00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:26.750
<b>nor is he influenced by rajas, </b>
<b>i.e., desires and struggle,</b>

25
00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.541
<b>and yes,</b>

26
00:02:27.541 --> 00:02:31.458
<b>his goal is not even sattva, i.e., peace.</b>

27
00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:33.875
<b>He has no such goal at all.</b>

28
00:02:33.875 --> 00:02:38.833
<b>He has only one goal, to surrender to God,</b>

29
00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:43.500
<b>and he acts only with this feeling.</b>

30
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.083
<b>The second word -</b>

31
00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:47.791
<b>jñānāvasthitacetasaḥ -</b>

32
00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:51.000
<b>meaning situated in divine knowledge –</b>

33
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.083
<b>such a person has a deep </b>
<b>knowledge of spiritual truth.</b>

34
00:02:55.083 --> 00:02:58.625
<b>He knows that if everything </b>
<b>belongs to Lord Krishna,</b>

35
00:02:58.625 --> 00:03:00.541
<b>everything has been given by Him,</b>

36
00:03:00.541 --> 00:03:07.708
<b>then he cannot dedicate the fruit of his</b>
<b>actions to anyone other than Him.</b>

37
00:03:07.708 --> 00:03:08.833
<b>The third word -</b>

38
00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:11.416
<b>samagraṁ pravilīyate –</b>

39
00:03:11.416 --> 00:03:16.375
<b>meaning the dissolution of all actions into the transcendental divinity –</b>

40
00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:19.250
<b>because his every action is dedicated to God,</b>

41
00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.416
<b>he has no attachment to any good or bad result,</b>

42
00:03:23.416 --> 00:03:32.166
<b>then in a way all the fruits of his actions</b>
<b>become zero, completely dissolved.</b>

43
00:03:32.166 --> 00:03:35.416
<b>Then in the twenty-fourth (24th) verse,</b>
<b>Lord Krishna says</b>

44
00:03:35.416 --> 00:03:38.583
<b>that such a person performs action </b>
<b>considering it as a sacrifice,</b>

45
00:03:38.583 --> 00:03:42.291
<b>a sacrifice in which the offering is also Brahma,</b>

46
00:03:42.291 --> 00:03:44.375
<b>the ghee is also Brahma,</b>

47
00:03:44.375 --> 00:03:46.291
<b>the fire is also Brahma,</b>

48
00:03:46.291 --> 00:03:50.125
<b>and the person performing it is also Brahma.</b>

49
00:03:50.125 --> 00:03:56.541
<b>And only the person who remains thus </b>
<b>absorbed in Brahma attains Brahma.</b>

50
00:03:56.541 --> 00:04:00.416
<b>Here, you can also understand Brahma as God.</b>

51
00:04:00.416 --> 00:04:02.500
<b>But action being a sacrifice?</b>

52
00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:07.708
<b>The offering, ghee, fire all being </b>
<b>God in the sacrifice?</b>

53
00:04:07.708 --> 00:04:09.916
<b>Let's understand this.</b>

54
00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:13.625
<b>A sacrifice mainly has four parts...</b>

55
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:14.458
<b>the fire,</b>

56
00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:15.416
<b>the ghee,</b>

57
00:04:15.416 --> 00:04:17.875
<b>the offering that is made,</b>

58
00:04:17.875 --> 00:04:21.500
<b>and the person who performs the sacrifice.</b>

59
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:28.500
<b>A person situated in divine knowledge believes </b>
<b>that Brahma, God, is in every particle of the world.</b>

60
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.750
<b>For example,</b>

61
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:33.708
<b>Arjuna can also fight this </b>
<b>war considering it a sacrifice,</b>

62
00:04:33.708 --> 00:04:37.416
<b>a sacrifice where the fire is his firm determination</b>

63
00:04:37.416 --> 00:04:39.875
<b>that keeps this sacrifice blazing,</b>

64
00:04:39.875 --> 00:04:44.291
<b>the materials like ghee are the </b>
<b>weapons that are his aids,</b>

65
00:04:44.291 --> 00:04:50.041
<b>in this sacrifice, the warriors who will </b>
<b>attain heroic ascension are being offered,</b>

66
00:04:50.041 --> 00:04:54.333
<b>and ultimately it is Arjuna himself who </b>
<b>is performing this sacrifice.</b>

67
00:04:54.333 --> 00:04:57.583
<b>But if this is seen from the perspective </b>
<b>of divine knowledge,</b>

68
00:04:57.583 --> 00:05:00.500
<b>then Brahma, God, is in every particle.</b>

69
00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:04.333
<b>God is in Arjuna too, He is in his weapons too,</b>

70
00:05:04.333 --> 00:05:09.125
<b>God is in all those warriors who will be offered.</b>

71
00:05:09.125 --> 00:05:13.333
<b>And the one who, being thus absorbed in God, </b>
<b>will consider every action as a sacrifice,</b>

72
00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:16.750
<b>will consider every part of the</b>
<b>sacrifice as a part of God,</b>

73
00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.375
<b>has undoubtedly attained God.</b>

74
00:05:20.375 --> 00:05:25.416
<b>In this way, when we completely </b>
<b>dedicate our life to God,</b>

75
00:05:25.416 --> 00:05:29.625
<b>our every action becomes a spiritual sacrifice,</b>

76
00:05:29.625 --> 00:05:34.708
<b>which leads us to liberation and the divine realm.</b>

77
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:46.791
<b>These verses talk about sacrifice, about offering.</b>

78
00:05:46.791 --> 00:05:56.000
<b>If you want to experience true </b>
<b>spirituality in life, to live a liberated life,</b>

79
00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.791
<b>then see your actions as a sacrifice, an offering.</b>

80
00:06:01.791 --> 00:06:06.625
<b>Which is done only with a sense of dedication.</b>

81
00:06:06.625 --> 00:06:13.125
<b>Whether it is your daily activities, </b>
<b>your behavior with others,</b>

82
00:06:13.125 --> 00:06:18.166
<b>or even your goals or objectives.</b>

83
00:06:18.166 --> 00:06:22.500
<b>Just as the fire of sacrifice brings purification,</b>

84
00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.166
<b>similarly,</b>

85
00:06:24.166 --> 00:06:33.583
<b>every action done considering it as service </b>
<b>or sacrifice also purifies your personality.</b>

86
00:06:33.583 --> 00:06:43.583
<b>Act with the belief that behind your every </b>
<b>small action there is also a divine purpose,</b>

87
00:06:43.583 --> 00:06:47.875
<b>which is in accordance with God's will.</b>

88
00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:53.875
<b>This perspective will make your</b>
<b>every action, every relationship, every activity</b>

89
00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:59.416
<b>a stepping stone towards spiritual progress.</b>

90
00:06:59.416 --> 00:07:03.625
<b>When you look at your </b>
<b>actions from this perspective,</b>

91
00:07:03.625 --> 00:07:10.250
<b>you become free from personal </b>
<b>gain and fear of failure,</b>

92
00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:14.416
<b>and your actions become sacred.</b>

93
00:07:19.333 --> 00:07:22.625
<b>There are many beautiful things in this verse,</b>

94
00:07:22.625 --> 00:07:32.625
<b>such as seeing every action as a sacrifice, </b>
<b>dedicating every action like an offering. </b>

95
00:07:32.625 --> 00:07:38.833
<b>All this is extremely helpful in</b>
<b>the family environment.</b>

96
00:07:38.833 --> 00:07:43.750
<b>Encourage family members to see their </b>
<b>every duty,</b>

97
00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:54.333
<b>every task not as a heavy responsibility, </b>
<b>but as a service being dedicated to others.</b>

98
00:07:54.333 --> 00:07:59.625
<b>It is indeed true, whether it is raising children,</b>

99
00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:01.583
<b>taking care of the house,</b>

100
00:08:01.583 --> 00:08:04.458
<b>earning a livelihood through hard work</b>

101
00:08:04.458 --> 00:08:09.875
<b>or making your parents </b>
<b>proud through hard work –</b>

102
00:08:09.875 --> 00:08:15.916
<b>all these actions are in a way </b>
<b>service to family members.</b>

103
00:08:15.916 --> 00:08:24.958
<b>This perspective gives even the seemingly </b>
<b>ordinary family duties a higher spiritual form.</b>

104
00:08:24.958 --> 00:08:27.958
<b>Also reflect on this perspective,</b>

105
00:08:27.958 --> 00:08:32.750
<b>and encourage family members towards it.</b>

106
00:08:37.041 --> 00:08:38.291
<b>Dedication,</b>

107
00:08:38.291 --> 00:08:47.875
<b>spirit of service and having a divine </b>
<b>purpose even in the smallest of actions.</b>

108
00:08:47.875 --> 00:08:49.666
<b>From these two verses,</b>

109
00:08:49.666 --> 00:08:55.250
<b>you can definitely adopt these </b>
<b>lessons for professional life.</b>

110
00:08:55.250 --> 00:09:01.750
<b>Encourage yourself, as well as</b>
<b>the people working under you,</b>

111
00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:07.791
<b>to see professional activities not only </b>
<b>from the perspective of material success,</b>

112
00:09:07.791 --> 00:09:12.541
<b>but as a larger purpose.</b>

113
00:09:12.541 --> 00:09:14.041
<b>Think,</b>

114
00:09:14.041 --> 00:09:18.583
<b>what is the core purpose of every organization? </b>

115
00:09:18.583 --> 00:09:24.250
<b>To fulfill the needs of customers, </b>
<b>to make their life simpler.</b>

116
00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:29.000
<b>So from that perspective, every </b>
<b>person working in the organization</b>

117
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:33.666
<b>is doing their part towards this big purpose,</b>

118
00:09:33.666 --> 00:09:37.041
<b>making someone's life simpler.</b>

119
00:09:37.041 --> 00:09:46.458
<b>This shifts your thinking from small personal </b>
<b>gains and losses towards social welfare.</b>

120
00:09:46.458 --> 00:09:49.166
<b>No work remains small.</b>

121
00:09:49.166 --> 00:09:52.583
<b>If you are in a leadership position,</b>

122
00:09:52.583 --> 00:09:56.958
<b>create such an environment in your organization</b>

123
00:09:56.958 --> 00:10:04.666
<b>where people make collective welfare</b>
<b>their focal point rather than personal ambitions.</b>

124
00:10:04.666 --> 00:10:12.875
<b>To encourage this, honor mutual </b>
<b>cooperation and collective efforts.</b>

125
00:10:12.875 --> 00:10:14.333
<b>Also,</b>

126
00:10:14.333 --> 00:10:19.791
<b>understand the higher purpose of the </b>
<b>thinking adopted by the organization,</b>

127
00:10:19.791 --> 00:10:22.625
<b>and follow it.</b>

128
00:10:22.625 --> 00:10:29.541
<b>There is a higher purpose of service and human </b>
<b>welfare hidden in every activity of the organization.</b>

129
00:10:29.541 --> 00:10:30.833
<b>Understand this,</b>

130
00:10:30.833 --> 00:10:36.000
<b>and encourage others too </b>
<b>towards this perspective.</b>

